1. Implementation
I implemented two methods to find the nearest neighbor: Brute Force and K-d Tree. Brute Force checks every point and finds the one with the smallest distance. K-d Tree organizes points into a binary tree. It uses the median to split the points and changes the splitting dimension at each level.
During the search, K-d Tree first searches the closer branch. It also checks the other branch if there could be a closer point.

2. Testing
I wrote five tests to check my implementation. All five tests passed.
The tests covered normal nearest neighbor search, one point, an empty tree, backtracking, and 3D points.

